  {
    "id": "A.20",
    "statement": "For a simply connected noncontractible two-dimensional W with rank H2=kappa, dimension-two R2 resolutions are impossible at mu >= max(aleph0,kappa)^aleph0. For W=S2 this excludes mu >= continuum. For W=vee_lambda S2 with infinite lambda^aleph0=lambda the exact threshold is mu<lambda.",
    "status": "Proved",
    "where_proved": "sections/A_dimension_frontier.tex",
    "depends_on": "A.13; A.19",
    "manuscript_pages_settled": "",
    "notes": "Unrestricted dimension-two existence is refuted. The S2 interval aleph0 <= mu < continuum remains undecided and is retained in A.U1."
  }
